IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sga2-nouns`
IMPORT `sga2-s76-whitewash`

-- Tests for sga2-s76-whitewash.l4: s 76(9A), (9B), (9BA), (9C), (9CA) and (9D) of the Companies Act 1967 (Singapore).
-- Expected values are written from the text (inputs/CoA1967.txt lines 7590-7812), beside each assertion, before the code was run.
-- Calendar facts used: 5 October 2026 is a Monday; 9, 16 October 2026 are Fridays; 15 October 2026 is a Thursday; "business day" counts every day but Saturday, Sunday and the listed public holidays (s 4(1)).
-- An answer NOTHING for a route means: a condition is not met, so the paragraph says nothing and s 76(1) decides.

§ `Solvency statements made up from the text of s 7A`

-- A solvency statement for the financial assistance, signed by all 3 of 3 directors (s 7A(1) and (2)).
`a statement signed by every director` MEANS `Solvency statement` WITH
    `the proposal it concerns` IS `a giving of financial assistance under section 76(9A) or (9B)`
    `the date of the statement` IS Date 1 10 2026
    `it is a statement by the directors of the company` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that, as regards the company's situation at its date, there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of winding up` IS FALSE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months immediately after its date` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets will not, after the proposal, become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS TRUE
    `the directors intend to commence winding up of the company within the 12 months immediately after its date` IS FALSE
    `the number of directors of the company` IS 3
    `the number of directors who have signed it as a written declaration` IS 3
    `it is accompanied by a report from the company's auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances` IS FALSE

-- Signed by 2 of 3 directors and no auditor report: not in the form s 7A(2) requires.
`a statement signed by two of three directors with no auditor report` MEANS `Solvency statement` WITH
    `the proposal it concerns` IS `a giving of financial assistance under section 76(9A) or (9B)`
    `the date of the statement` IS Date 1 10 2026
    `it is a statement by the directors of the company` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that, as regards the company's situation at its date, there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of winding up` IS FALSE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months immediately after its date` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets will not, after the proposal, become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS TRUE
    `the directors intend to commence winding up of the company within the 12 months immediately after its date` IS FALSE
    `the number of directors of the company` IS 3
    `the number of directors who have signed it as a written declaration` IS 2
    `it is accompanied by a report from the company's auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances` IS FALSE

-- Signed by 2 of 3 but accompanied by the auditor report: in the form s 7A(2)(b) allows.
`a statement signed by two of three directors with an auditor report` MEANS `Solvency statement` WITH
    `the proposal it concerns` IS `a giving of financial assistance under section 76(9A) or (9B)`
    `the date of the statement` IS Date 1 10 2026
    `it is a statement by the directors of the company` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that, as regards the company's situation at its date, there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of winding up` IS FALSE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months immediately after its date` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets will not, after the proposal, become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS TRUE
    `the directors intend to commence winding up of the company within the 12 months immediately after its date` IS FALSE
    `the number of directors of the company` IS 3
    `the number of directors who have signed it as a written declaration` IS 2
    `it is accompanied by a report from the company's auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances` IS TRUE

-- A statement about some other proposal.
`a statement for another proposal` MEANS `Solvency statement` WITH
    `the proposal it concerns` IS `some other proposal`
    `the date of the statement` IS Date 1 10 2026
    `it is a statement by the directors of the company` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that, as regards the company's situation at its date, there is no ground on which the company could then be found to be unable to pay its debts` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after the commencement of winding up` IS FALSE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the company will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months immediately after its date` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets is not less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS TRUE
    `it says the directors have formed the opinion that the value of the company's assets will not, after the proposal, become less than the value of its liabilities (including contingent liabilities)` IS TRUE
    `the directors intend to commence winding up of the company within the 12 months immediately after its date` IS FALSE
    `the number of directors of the company` IS 3
    `the number of directors who have signed it as a written declaration` IS 3
    `it is accompanied by a report from the company's auditor that the auditor has inquired into the affairs of the company and is of the opinion that the statement is not unreasonable given all the circumstances` IS FALSE

§ `s 76(9A)(a): within 10 percent of paid-up capital and reserves`

-- Paid-up capital 600 and reserves 400 make 1,000; 10% is 100. "would not exceed 10%": exactly 100 is within it; 101 is not.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(a) the assistance is within 10 percent of paid-up capital and reserves` 100 0 600 400 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(a) the assistance is within 10 percent of paid-up capital and reserves` 101 0 600 400 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(a) the assistance is within 10 percent of paid-up capital and reserves` 1 0 600 400 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "together with any other financial assistance given by the company under this subsection repayment of which remains outstanding": 60 and 40 make 100; 60 and 41 make 101.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(a) the assistance is within 10 percent of paid-up capital and reserves` 60 40 600 400 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(a) the assistance is within 10 percent of paid-up capital and reserves` 60 41 600 400 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The figures must be those "disclosed in the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201".
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(a) the assistance is within 10 percent of paid-up capital and reserves` 100 0 600 400 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 76(9A)(b) to (e)`

#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(b) the company receives fair value` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(b) the company receives fair value` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c): the board passes a resolution that (i) the company should give the assistance, (ii) it is in the best interests of the company, (iii) the terms are fair and reasonable.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(c) the board has passed the resolution the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(c) the board has passed the resolution the paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(c) the board has passed the resolution the paragraph requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(c) the board has passed the resolution the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(c) the board has passed the resolution the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(d) the resolution sets out the grounds` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(d) the resolution sets out the grounds` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (e): all the directors make a solvency statement in relation to the giving of the financial assistance (the statement must be one under s 7A(1) and (2)).
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(e) all the directors have made a solvency statement` `a statement signed by every director` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(e) all the directors have made a solvency statement` `a statement signed by every director` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Signed by two of three directors with no auditor report: not in the form s 7A(2) requires, so not a solvency statement.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(e) all the directors have made a solvency statement` `a statement signed by two of three directors with no auditor report` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Two of three signed but accompanied by the auditor's report (s 7A(2)(b)): in the form.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(e) all the directors have made a solvency statement` `a statement signed by two of three directors with an auditor report` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A company exempt from audit under s 205B or 205C needs every director's signature (s 7A(2)(a)): two of three with a report is not enough.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(e) all the directors have made a solvency statement` `a statement signed by two of three directors with an auditor report` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A statement about some other proposal is not a statement in relation to the giving of financial assistance.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(e) all the directors have made a solvency statement` `a statement for another proposal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 76(9A)(f): the notice to each member within 10 business days of providing the assistance`

-- Provided Monday 5 October 2026; no public holidays: the 10th business day is Monday 19 October 2026.
-- Arguments: day provided; day the notice was sent; notice sent; class and number; consideration; identity; nature and amount; public holidays.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 19 10 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 20 10 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- With Tuesday 13 October 2026 a public holiday the 10th business day is Tuesday 20 October.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 20 10 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (LIST (Date 13 10 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 21 10 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (LIST (Date 13 10 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Provided on Friday 9 October 2026: Friday 23 October is the 10th business day; Saturday 24 and Monday 26 are late.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 9 10 2026) (Date 23 10 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 9 10 2026) (Date 24 10 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 9 10 2026) (Date 26 10 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A notice sent on the day the assistance is provided is not later than the end of the period: counts (fork F-A8).
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 5 10 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No notice sent, or a notice missing one of the four particulars.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 6 10 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 6 10 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 6 10 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 6 10 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(f) the company has sent each member the notice in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 6 10 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 76(9A)(g): the copies lodged with the Registrar by the next business day`

-- Notice sent Friday 16 October 2026: the business day next following is Monday 19 October.
-- Arguments: day the notice was sent; day lodged; a copy of the notice lodged; a copy of the solvency statement lodged; public holidays.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(g) the company has lodged the copies with the Registrar in time` (Date 16 10 2026) (Date 19 10 2026) TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(g) the company has lodged the copies with the Registrar in time` (Date 16 10 2026) (Date 20 10 2026) TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Monday 19 October a public holiday: Tuesday 20 October is the business day next following.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(g) the company has lodged the copies with the Registrar in time` (Date 16 10 2026) (Date 20 10 2026) TRUE TRUE (LIST (Date 19 10 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(g) the company has lodged the copies with the Registrar in time` (Date 16 10 2026) (Date 21 10 2026) TRUE TRUE (LIST (Date 19 10 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Notice sent Monday 5 October: Tuesday 6 October is the business day next following.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(g) the company has lodged the copies with the Registrar in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 6 10 2026) TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(g) the company has lodged the copies with the Registrar in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 7 10 2026) TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Both copies must be lodged.
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(g) the company has lodged the copies with the Registrar in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 6 10 2026) FALSE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A)(g) the company has lodged the copies with the Registrar in time` (Date 5 10 2026) (Date 6 10 2026) TRUE FALSE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 76(9A) as a whole`

#ASSERT `s 76(9A) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9A) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76(9A) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76(9A) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76(9A) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76(9A) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76(9A) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76(9A) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

