§ `s 76(9BA): the route where the assistance does not materially prejudice`

-- (a): "does not materially prejudice (i) the interests of the company or its shareholders; or (ii) the company's ability to pay its creditors": prejudice to either defeats it (fork F-A10).
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(a) giving the assistance does not materially prejudice the company, its shareholders or its creditors` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(a) giving the assistance does not materially prejudice the company, its shareholders or its creditors` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(a) giving the assistance does not materially prejudice the company, its shareholders or its creditors` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(a) giving the assistance does not materially prejudice the company, its shareholders or its creditors` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): the board passes a resolution that (i) the company should give the assistance and (ii) the terms are fair and reasonable (no "best interests" limb).
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(b) the board has passed the resolution the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(b) the board has passed the resolution the paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(b) the board has passed the resolution the paragraph requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(b) the board has passed the resolution the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(c) the resolution sets out the grounds` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(c) the resolution sets out the grounds` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(d) the company has lodged a copy of the resolution with the Registrar` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA)(d) the company has lodged a copy of the resolution with the Registrar` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76(9BA) subsection (1) does not prohibit the giving of the assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 76(9C) and (9CA): what ends the routes before the assistance is given`

-- (9C) arguments: the assistance is to be given under (9A) or (9B); a voting director ceased to be satisfied it is in the best interests; ... ceased to be satisfied the terms are fair; a director no longer has reasonable grounds.
#ASSERT `s 76(9C) the company is barred from giving the assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9C) the company is barred from giving the assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9C) the company is barred from giving the assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9C) the company is barred from giving the assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not given under (9A) or (9B): the bar speaks only of those routes.
#ASSERT `s 76(9C) the company is barred from giving the assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B)` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (9CA): under (9BA), a voting director ceased to be satisfied that the terms are fair and reasonable.
#ASSERT `s 76(9CA) the company is barred from giving the assistance under subsection (9BA)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(9CA) the company is barred from giving the assistance under subsection (9BA)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9CA) the company is barred from giving the assistance under subsection (9BA)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The forbidden act of (9C) and of (9CA) is BREACH; with no event the prohibition stands.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 76(9C) a company must not give the assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B) once a director has ceased to be satisfied` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY (Company "Acme Pte Ltd") DOES `s 76(9C) give financial assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B) after a director has ceased to be satisfied or no longer has reasonable grounds` AT 6

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 76(9C) a company must not give the assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B) once a director has ceased to be satisfied` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 9)

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 76(9CA) a company must not give the assistance under subsection (9BA) once a director has ceased to be satisfied` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY (Company "Acme Pte Ltd") DOES `s 76(9CA) give financial assistance under subsection (9BA) after a director has ceased to be satisfied that the terms are fair and reasonable` AT 6

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 76(9CA) a company must not give the assistance under subsection (9BA) once a director has ceased to be satisfied` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 9)

§ `s 76(9D): directors' duties are not relieved`

-- "A director ... is not relieved of any duty ... by (a) the passing of a resolution by the board under (9A) or (9BA); or (b) the passing of a resolution by the board and by the members under (9B)": a flat negative.
#ASSERT `s 76(9D) the director is relieved of the director's duty to the company by the resolution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9D) the director is relieved of the director's duty to the company by the resolution` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(9D) the director is relieved of the director's duty to the company by the resolution` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
